# TextFSM template: MikroTik RouterOS 7.x
# `/routing bgp session print detail`.
#
# RouterOS 7.x's BGP session has a per-entry detail print form:
#
#  Flags: E - established, * - dynamic
#   0 E name="peer1"
#       remote.address=10.0.0.2 .as=65001 .id=10.0.0.2 .refresh=yes
#       local.address=10.0.0.1 .as=65000 .role=ebgp
#       output.network="bgp-networks" .filter-chain="" .accepted-routes=600
#       input.filter="bgp-in" .accepted-routes=500 .rejected-routes=0 .ignored-routes=0
#       hold-time=3m keepalive-time=1m uptime=1d2h3m4s
#       prefix-count=500
#   1 name="peer2"
#       remote.address=10.0.0.3 .as=65002 .id=0.0.0.0 .refresh=no
#       local.address=10.0.0.1 .as=65000 .role=ebgp
#       hold-time=3m keepalive-time=1m uptime=0s
#       prefix-count=0
#
# Capture strategy:
#   - The leading `E` flag column marks established sessions. We
#     capture it directly into `state` via two distinct entry-header
#     patterns (one with the `E` flag, one without). The projector
#     normalises `E` → "established" and the empty state for non-
#     Established peers stays empty (UI shows it as "idle"-ish).
#   - The `remote.address` / `.as` line is the canonical anchor: it
#     always carries peer IP and ASN.
#   - The `prefix-count` line is the last per-entry line we care
#     about and triggers Record. The `output.…accepted-routes=N`
#     and `input.…accepted-routes=N` lines (which only appear on
#     Established sessions) populate prefixes_sent / received.
Value Required peer_ip ([0-9a-fA-F:.]+)
Value peer_asn (\d+)
Value description (\S+)
Value uptime (\S+)
Value prefixes_received (\d+)
Value prefixes_sent (\d+)
Value state (E)

Start
  ^\s*Flags:\s+E\s+-\s+established
  # Established entry header — captures the `E` flag into `state`.
  ^\s*\d+\s+${state}\s+name="${description}"\s*$$
  # Non-Established entry header — `state` stays empty.
  ^\s*\d+\s+name="${description}"\s*$$
  ^\s+remote\.address=${peer_ip}\s+\.as=${peer_asn}
  ^\s+output\..*\.accepted-routes=${prefixes_sent}
  ^\s+input\..*\.accepted-routes=${prefixes_received}
  ^\s+hold-time=\S+\s+keepalive-time=\S+\s+uptime=${uptime}
  ^\s+prefix-count=\d+\s*$$ -> Record
